      "content": "During pre‑flight, verify that the pitot‑static system is clean and unobstructed: look at the pitot tube tip for insects or debris, and gently clear the static ports with a clean probe or your finger. Confirm that the pitot‑heat switches (if equipped) are operational and that the heating elements glow when turned on. Check that the airspeed, altimeter, and vertical‑speed indicators all move together when you change the aircraft’s attitude (e.g., pitch up and down) and that they respond correctly to a calibrated pressure source or a handheld pitot‑static tester. Finally, inspect the cockpit for any loose instrument wiring, cracked tubing, or missing pitot‑tube covers that could allow moisture or insects to enter.",
